os-dhcp-interface-ha lets an existing active/passive OPNsense CARP pair move one
IPv4 DHCP client interface between nodes. A WAN is the common use case, but
any eligible logical interface can be selected.

The plugin does not implement a second HA election protocol and does not
replace OPNsense DHCP, routing, NAT, PF, pfsync, or CARP.  It provides a
stable logical interface, a shared ordinary unicast MAC identity, and
fail-closed Layer-2 fencing of the local carrier.

This package is experimental.  Production deployment remains gated by
the prototype tests documented in docs/dhcp-interface-ha.md.

